## Layer-by-Layer Breakdown

[tabs]
[tab title="Client & CDN"]

### Client Devices
Netflix supports every major device category through a unified ELB entry point.

[table cols="Device Type,Examples,Protocol"
  Mobile       | iOS / Android          | HTTPS / HLS
  Smart TV     | Samsung / LG / Roku    | HTTPS / DASH
  Web Browser  | Chrome / Safari        | HTTPS / MSE
  Game Console | Xbox / PlayStation     | HTTPS / HLS
]

### OpenConnect CDN
[callout icon=☁️ title="OpenConnect" text="Netflix's proprietary CDN. Video bytes are served directly from ISP-embedded appliances — not the origin servers. This offloads ~95% of traffic before it hits the API gateway." color=purple]

[progress label="Traffic served by OpenConnect" value=95 color=purple]
[progress label="Traffic hitting origin (API)" value=5 color=gray]

[/tab]
[tab title="API Gateway (ZUUL)"]

### ZUUL Gateway Components

[table cols="Component,Role,Key Capability"
  ELB               | Entry point load balancer      | Health checks, SSL termination
  Netty Server      | Non-blocking I/O server        | High concurrency, async I/O
  Inbound Filter    | Pre-routing request processing | Auth, rate limiting, logging
  Endpoint Filter   | Business logic routing         | Request routing to microservices
  Outbound Filter   | Post-routing response handling | Response transformation, compression
]

[callout icon=🔀 title="Request Flow" text="REQUEST: Client → ELB → Netty → Inbound Filter → Endpoint Filter → Microservices. RESPONSE: Microservices → Endpoint Filter → Outbound Filter → Netty → Client." color=blue]

[/tab]
[tab title="Microservices"]

### Resilience Patterns

[table cols="Component,Pattern,Purpose"
  Hystrix        | Circuit Breaker     | Stops cascade failures — fallback when service is down
  Service Client | Client-side LB      | Smart routing to healthy microservice instances
  EV Cache       | Distributed Cache   | Memcached-based, reduces DB load significantly
  Cassandra      | Wide-column DB      | User data, viewing history, profiles
  MySQL          | Relational DB       | Billing and payment data
]

[callout icon=⚡ title="Hystrix Circuit Breaker" text="If a downstream microservice fails repeatedly, Hystrix opens the circuit and returns a fallback. This prevents one slow service from cascading into a full outage." color=red]

[progress label="Hystrix fault tolerance coverage" value=100 color=green]
[progress label="Target microservice availability" value=99 color=blue]

[/tab]
[tab title="Event Processing"]

### Event Pipeline

[timeline color=yellow]
- Endpoint Filter: Emits events for every API call
- Chukwa: Collects and aggregates logs from all services
- S3: Raw event storage — durable, cheap, scalable
- EMR / Hadoop: Batch analytics on raw event data
- Kafka: Real-time event stream ingestion
- Apache Samza: Stream processing and message routing
- Elasticsearch: Search and real-time log querying
- Spark: Machine learning and large-scale data processing
[/timeline]

[chart type=doughnut title="Event Pipeline Use Cases"
  Analytics=35 Monitoring=25 ML=20 Search=15 Alerting=5
]

[/tab]
[tab title="Video Pipeline"]

### Content Ingestion

[table cols="Stage,Component,Detail"
  1. Ingest    | New Video Upload    | Studio delivers raw master files
  2. Validate  | Validation Service  | Quality check, metadata extraction
  3. Transcode | Transcoder Workers  | Encodes 1200+ versions per title
  4. Queue     | Queue               | Manages async worker job dispatch
  5. Store     | Amazon S3           | Stores all encoded versions
  6. Serve     | OpenConnect CDN     | Distributed to ISP edge nodes
]

[callout icon=🎬 title="Encoding Scale" text="Every Netflix title is encoded into 1,200+ variants — different resolutions (240p to 4K), bitrates, audio tracks, and subtitle formats. Handled by thousands of concurrent async Transcoder workers." color=blue]

[/tab]
[tab title="Chaos Engineering"]

### Resilience Testing

[table cols="Tool,Purpose,How It Works"
  Chaos Monkey  | Service failure injection | Randomly terminates production instances
  TITUS         | Container management      | Schedules and isolates service containers
]

[callout icon=🐒 title="Chaos Monkey" text="Chaos Monkey randomly kills production services during business hours. If your system can't survive a random kill, it can't survive a real failure. Netflix runs this in prod — daily." color=red]

[alert type=info text="Chaos Monkey is part of the Simian Army — a suite of chaos tools that also includes Latency Monkey, Conformity Monkey, and Janitor Monkey."]

[/tab]
[/tabs]

[divider]

## Key Design Decisions

[columns]
[col]
[kpi label="Microservices" value="500+" target="Independent deploys" color=blue]
[/col]
[col]
[kpi label="Uptime SLA" value="99.99%" target="<1h downtime/year" color=green]
[/col]
[col]
[kpi label="CDN Offload" value="95%" target="Origin traffic reduction" color=purple]
[/col]
[/columns]

[section title="Architectural Trade-offs" style=card]

[callout icon=✅ title="What This Architecture Gets Right" text="Full decoupling between content delivery (CDN), API routing (ZUUL), business logic (microservices), and analytics (event pipeline). Each layer scales independently and fails independently." color=green]

[callout icon=⚠️ title="Complexity Cost" text="500+ microservices means distributed tracing, service discovery, and network overhead become critical engineering challenges. Hystrix, EV Cache, and Cassandra add significant operational burden." color=yellow]

[callout icon=🔑 title="The Key Insight" text="Netflix solved the CAP theorem tradeoff by accepting eventual consistency for non-critical data (viewing history, recommendations) while enforcing strong consistency only for billing (MySQL)." color=blue]

[/section]

[divider]

## Technology Stack Summary

[table cols="Layer,Technology,Why"
  Load Balancing    | AWS ELB           | Managed, integrates with AWS ecosystem
  API Gateway       | ZUUL + Netty      | Non-blocking I/O handles millions of concurrent connections
  Circuit Breaker   | Hystrix           | Prevents cascade failures in microservice mesh
  Primary DB        | Cassandra         | Linear scalability, multi-region replication
  Billing DB        | MySQL             | ACID compliance for financial transactions
  Cache             | EVCache           | Memcached-based, reduces Cassandra load by ~90%
  Stream Processing | Kafka + Samza     | Real-time event processing at millions of events/sec
  Batch Processing  | S3 + EMR + Spark  | Nightly ML model retraining, analytics
  Search / Logs     | Elasticsearch     | Sub-second log search across all services
  CDN               | OpenConnect       | Proprietary ISP-embedded appliances
  Chaos             | Chaos Monkey      | Proactive resilience validation in production
]
